; edworld's settings: edworld makes this file by itself at its first start, with all its settings; a copy of this one
; is for setting something before that. Every line here is a comment holding edworld's default.
;
; Copy it as edworld.ini (without .example):
;   - on its own: into the game's folder, Products\elite-dangerous-odyssey-64, beside edworld's d3d11.dll
;   - through edloader: into edloader\config
; Take the ';' off the start of a line to change it; a change takes a new start of the game.
; Comments stand on lines of their own. All the settings: doc/users.md.

; Where edworld goes on to, the next d3d11 mod; empty = the system's own. Through edloader, with other mods after edworld in edloader.txt: d3d11.dll. On its own, a mod's dll you renamed: d3d11_edhm.dll
;next = 

; The game's Status.json, the journals beside it; change it only if edworld looks in the wrong place
;status_file = C:\Users\you\Saved Games\Frontier Developments\Elite Dangerous\Status.json

; Clouds over planets with an atmosphere: 0 = none
;clouds = 1

; the layer's height over the surface, as a part of the planet's radius
;clouds_height = 0.005

; how much they cover what is under them, 0 to 1
;clouds_alpha = 0.45

; how much of the sky they take, 0 clear to 1 overcast
;clouds_cover = 0.55

; how much of the sun they give back
;clouds_light = 0.4

; Clouds with depth you fly through: 0 = the flat layer, lighter for a weaker graphics card
;clouds_volume = 1
;clouds_bottom = 0.003
;clouds_top = 0.012
;clouds_steps = 32
;clouds_density = 1.2
;clouds_opacity = 0.75

; the star's light the clouds with depth get at least, so a faint star does not lose them; 0 = as the game gives it
;clouds_min_light = 400

; how much lighter the clouds with depth are seen from under them, 1 = as they are
;clouds_under_gain = 2

; how much the fine shape near you cuts the clouds with depth, 0 = none: a smooth fog from the ground
;clouds_detail = 1
;clouds_detail_size = 3000
;clouds_detail_range = 500000
;clouds_detail_edge = 8

; how much clear sky there is among the clouds with depth near you, from under them too; more = thinner, the view from orbit stays
;clouds_detail_gap = 0.14

; the wind in km/h at the floor of the clouds with depth and at their top; both 0 = still clouds
;clouds_wind_low = 100
;clouds_wind_high = 400

; how much lighter the clouds with depth are seen from above, 1 = as from under them
;clouds_top_gain = 2

; The navballs beside the radar: 0 = none, the game's compass is not read at all
;compass = 1

; The destination's factions under the jump panel: 0 = never ask EDSM
;edsm = 1

; how much the list's box covers what is behind it, 0 to 1
;list_alpha = 0.65

